# Cline Rules for WorkitPT

You are working in a production-intended mobile marketplace repository.

Always read `AGENTS.md` first, then `docs/TECH_STACK_ELEVATION_PLAN.md`.

## Active Folders

- `workitpt/` - Flutter mobile app.
- `workitptproject/` - TypeScript backend API.
- `docs/` - architecture and handover documentation.
- `02-agent/`, `03-workflows/`, `04-prompting/`, `05-checklists/` - AI operating system.

## Do Not Touch Unless Asked

- `archive/`
- `.env`, `.env.*`
- signing files, keystores, private keys
- generated build outputs
- dependency folders

## Architecture Rules

- Keep Flutter/Dart unless an ADR changes the decision.
- Keep TypeScript backend direction.
- Backend payment work must use Stripe webhooks and idempotency.
- Backend must not receive raw card numbers or CVC.
- Future core data model should move toward PostgreSQL; do not deepen MongoDB coupling without documenting why.

## Work Style

- Make small changes.
- Run verification.
- Commit only clean, intentional diffs.
- Prefer documentation updates when architecture decisions change.
- Never guess around payments, auth, data migrations, or production secrets.
